# domain
- Viktor is an AI employee reachable at https://api.viktor.com through an OpenAI Chat Completions and Responses wire at <host>/api/compat/v1, an Anthropic Messages wire at <host>/api/compat, a hosted stateless Streamable-HTTP MCP server at <host>/mcp, and a native async REST API at <host>/api/public/v1
- a Core is the per-language shared package (TS `packages/core`, Py `python/core`) that owns the Viktor client, canonical message model, streaming parsing, error classification, and fixtures
- an Adapter is a thin per-framework package that depends on one Core and one upstream framework and only converts types and registers with the framework
- a RoutedToolId is a Viktor tool-call id of the form call_vk1_<thread>_<c|t|b>_<suffix> (toolu_vk1_… on the Anthropic wire) that embeds the durable thread id
- a Fixture is a recorded wire exchange (request, response or SSE frames) replayed in unit tests without network
- a LiveContractTest is a test that runs against the real Viktor API when VIKTOR_API_KEY is set and is skipped otherwise

# core/client
- label: the client reads VIKTOR_API_KEY and VIKTOR_BASE_URL (default https://api.viktor.com) from the environment when not given explicitly
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'reads VIKTOR_API_KEY and VIKTOR_BASE_URL'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- label: the client sends the key as `Authorization: Bearer` and always sends model `viktor`
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'sends bearer auth, forces model viktor'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- label: the TS core client exposes chat completions and responses (sync and streaming) with failure detection on both wires, anthropic messages, and list models
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'responses wire' && scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'assembles fragmented'
  tags: [implemented]
- label: adapters reach Viktor's native REST API only through the core's narrow client interface, so it can be re-implemented on the Viktor SDK without changing any adapter
  command: ! grep -rn 'api/public/v1' packages/ai-sdk/src packages/langchain/src packages/mastra/src packages/openai-agents/src python/langchain/src python/pydantic-ai/src python/openai-agents/src
  tags: [implemented]

