# maintenance
- label: a matrix runner tests any adapter against the min, latest and next versions of its framework, and the nightly workflow opens an issue instead of failing when only next breaks
  command: python3 scripts/upstream_matrix.py --list | grep -q 'pydantic-ai' && python3 scripts/upstream_matrix.py --adapter openai-agents-py --channel min >/dev/null 2>&1 && grep -q "continue-on-error: \${{ matrix.channel == 'next' }}" .github/workflows/upstream-matrix.yml && grep -q 'gh issue create' .github/workflows/upstream-matrix.yml
  tags: [implemented]
- label: every adapter README states the upstream versions it was tested against and the date
  command: for r in packages/ai-sdk packages/langchain packages/mastra packages/openai-agents python/langchain python/pydantic-ai python/openai-agents acp; do grep -q -i 'tested against' $r/README.md || { echo $r; exit 1; }; done
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the maintenance runbook states the expected ongoing cost, who breaks what, and the action for each CI signal
  command: grep -q 'Expected ongoing cost' docs/runbook.md && grep -q 'Signals and what to do' docs/runbook.md
  tags: [implemented, m6]
- label: the live contract workflow refuses to pass when the VIKTOR_API_KEY secret is missing, so skipped live tests can never look green
  command: grep -q 'refuse to pass without a key' .github/workflows/live.yml
  tags: [implemented, m6]
- label: live verification against production passed for both cores, all seven adapters, the MCP bridge and the ACP agent, and the evidence names what was not run live
  command: test $(ls fixtures/live/*.json | wc -l) -ge 12 && ! grep -rIlE 'zt_(live|test)_sk_[0-9a-f]{32}_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}' fixtures docs packages python mcp acp scripts spec upstream --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.venv
  tags: [implemented, live]

