## testing
- label: both cores parse every exchange recorded from the real Viktor API: chat, tool calls with routed ids, Responses with the thread id, Anthropic messages, and the 401 envelope
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/live-shapes.test.ts 'live recordings' && scripts/pt.sh viktor-integrations-core core/tests 'test_live_'
  tags: [implemented, live]

# protocols

## mcp
- label: the viktor-mcp bridge turns an HTTP auth failure into a JSON-RPC error that says what to fix
  command: scripts/vt.sh mcp/bridge test/bridge.test.ts 'auth failures'
  tags: [implemented, mcp]

## other
- label: viktor-acp answers the ACP initialize handshake over real stdio without an API key, as the ACP registry's CI requires
  command: cd acp && printf '%s\n' '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":0,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":1,"clientCapabilities":{}}}' | env -u VIKTOR_API_KEY timeout 5 node dist/cli.js 2>/dev/null | grep -q '"authMethods"'
  tags: [implemented, acp]
- label: viktor-acp reports a failed Viktor run as a request error carrying Viktor's message
  command: scripts/vt.sh acp test/agent.test.ts 'failed Viktor run'
  tags: [implemented, acp]
